        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681188" data-guid="7681188"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681188" data-guid="7681188" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681188_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">The provisions of this article apply to the administration and enforcement of the Uniform Code and of this Part <a class="xref" guid="7681181" href="7681181#7681181">2</a>.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681189"
      id="7681189"
      data-guid="7681189"
      data-position="3105"
      data-full-title="§ 133-47: Existing buildings."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681189_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681189_label" for="7681189_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681189"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-47
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681189"
    >
Existing buildings.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681189" data-guid="7681189"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681189" data-guid="7681189" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681189_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">No provision of this Part <a class="xref" guid="7681181" href="7681181#7681181">2</a> shall be construed to require any change in, alteration of or addition to a legally existing building or structure or the premises connected therewith, unless specifically so stated.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681190"
      id="7681190"
      data-guid="7681190"
      data-position="3106"
      data-full-title="§ 133-48: Department of Buildings and Regulatory Compliance."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681190_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681190_label" for="7681190_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681190"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-48
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681190"
    >
Department of Buildings and Regulatory Compliance.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681190" data-guid="7681190"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681190" data-guid="7681190" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681190_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="history">[Amended <span class="legref" data-ref=""><span class="hisdate">12-17-2012</span> by <span class="loclaw">L.L. No. 2-2012</span></span>]</div><div class="para">The function of the Department of Buildings and Regulatory Compliance shall consist of, but not necessarily be limited to, the review of applications and plans for building permits and the imposition and collection of the requisite fees therefor, together with all aspects of permits, licenses and inspections involving electric, plumbing, heating, ventilating and air-conditioning (HVAC) installations, elevators and all other building construction and occupancy issues and requirements under this Code and state law. The Department shall assume and be vested with all powers and duties previously exercised and performed by the Division of Buildings and Code and/or the Bureau of Buildings as set forth and established in Chapter 20, together with those enumerated in this Chapter <a class="xref" guid="7681109" href="7681109#7681109">133</a> (Building Construction) and Chapter <a class="xref" guid="7682800" href="7682800#7682800">231</a> (Housing) of this Code.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 27111253"
      id="27111253"
      data-guid="27111253"
      data-position="3107"
      data-full-title="§ 133-48.1: Commissioner; qualifications and appointment; vacancy."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="27111253_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="27111253_label" for="27111253_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#27111253"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 133-48.1
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="27111253"
